    "body": "> > Set currentNode to currentNode's parent in the [flat tree](https://drafts.csswg.org/css-scoping/#flat-tree).\r\n\r\nAhh, yep that would need an update. Conceptually the fix is easy, but it sounds like you think the flat tree machinery isn't there? I.e. something like this would fix it:\r\n\r\n> If currentNode is in the [flat tree](https://drafts.csswg.org/css-scoping/#flat-tree), then set currentNode to currentNode's parent in the [flat tree](https://drafts.csswg.org/css-scoping/#flat-tree). Otherwise set currentNode to null.\r\n\r\nIndeed that's how the implementation works already, for Chromium.",
